        <item>
            <title>0.27.9</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:04:07 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>69</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.27.9</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.27.9</h3><ul><li>Monitors now stay inside the access profiles of the session that owns them. A monitor made before its folder or app got an access profile, or taken over with claim_route, no longer brings mail from accounts that profile leaves out, and a session can still list, change and cancel its own monitors after its folder gets a profile.</li><li>Mail monitors can skip whole accounts: choose them under "Skip accounts" in Settings &gt; Monitors (agents: account_excludes).</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
